# K12

> K12, powered by Stride, Inc. (NYSE: LRN), has provided online education since 2000. K12 offers tuition-free online public schools in many states, tuition-based online private school, homeschool curriculum, tutoring, and career and college prep for students in grades K-12, plus online preschool.

Key facts:
- Online public schools powered by K12 are tuition-free for families. Availability depends on the student's state and district; use the School Finder to see options.
- K12 Private Academy and other private options are tuition-based and available nationwide and outside the U.S.
- Students learn with certified teachers trained in virtual instruction, a mix of scheduled live classes and self-paced work, and K12 curriculum. Most schools provide books and learning materials; some provide a computer.
- A parent or other responsible adult serves as the Learning Coach.
- K12 has served more than 3 million registered learners across its managed public schools, private schools, and Learning Solutions.
- Enrollment help: 866.968.7512. Spanish-language site: https://es.k12.com/

